This does not (yet) do any new work -- just moves the existing definitions to a new package.

Once moved, I we should revist the structure and some of the naming.  For example we have an object called "DrawStyle" that should likey be "GraphDrawStyle"


@sdboyer -- this removes the file in https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/main/cue/ui/gen.cue

Resolve https://github.com/opencollective/opencollective/issues/4567

Add all related models to the merge accounts util, to make sure we don't miss any data.

The goal of the `MigrationLogs` table is to be re-used whenever we need to store information about migration results. For example, we could imagine doing something like this in a sequelize migration:

```es6
await models.MigrationLog.create({
  type: 'MIGRATION',
  name: '20210615074327-platform-tip-debt-kind',
  data: {
    updatedTransactionsIds: [45,88,77]
  }
})
```

The real stuff happens in https://github.com/opencollective/opencollective-api/pull/6480/files#diff-5b651c29bc4624a4f05eb6a0ab745a233063e46ab263aca619d3cbeaf87a78ed.

As suggested in #470, the typecast operator from `oatpp::String` to `std::string` is included. 

Furthermore, to get `oatpp-swagger` running again, a case insensitive string comparison is required. For this purpose the `oatpp::String` class gets the following new methods:
```cpp
inline bool equalsCI(const std::string &sb) ;
inline bool equalsCI(const String &b);
inline bool equalsCI(const char *b);
```

Finally, trialling whitespaces are removed.

Closes: #470

