### Description
I've added a new parameter `urlMode` to the image cropper `.GetCropUrl()` extension methods in order to be able to select which url mode I need in that specific call, like it works now for `.Url()`.
In my case, I have the default url mode set to relative, but for things like the Open Graph image, I need it to be absolute.

I tested my changes by calling some of the extension methods from a view as follows

```
@Model.Image.GetCropUrl(1200, 620)
@Model.Image.GetCropUrl(1200, 620, urlMode: UrlMode.Absolute)
@Model.Image.GetCropUrl("crop1")
@Model.Image.GetCropUrl("crop1", UrlMode.Absolute)
```

